      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>This is the piyyuṭ for Yom Kippur known by its incipit שופט כל הארץ “Shofeṭ kol ha-Arets” (“Thou Judge of all the earth”) by the late 12th century payṭan, Shlomo ben Abun of France, as adapted in the form of a rhyming translation by Nina Salaman for <tei:hi rend="italic">Maḥzor Avodat Ohel Moed: Avodat Yom haKippurim vol. 2</tei:hi>, arranged and translated by Arthur Davis &amp; Herbert Adler (1904), p. 86. I have re-Hebraized the name “Jesse” to “Yishai.” –Aharon Varady</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_65408_notes"/>
